1
00:00:01,620 --> 00:00:03,860
What would you say if I told you I’m…

2
00:00:04,440 --> 00:00:06,340
not interested in the opposite sex?

3
00:00:06,860 --> 00:00:08,100
It’s Ruth, right?

4
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:12,000
Ji.

5
00:00:12,920 --> 00:00:14,470
Ji, is that you?

6
00:00:14,920 --> 00:00:18,110
Wow, you’re all grown up now.

7
00:00:18,650 --> 00:00:21,080
Is this Ms. Ornrampha?

8
00:00:22,090 --> 00:00:23,330
How do you know her, Ji?

9
00:02:04,930 --> 00:02:08,140
MR. JIRA, MS. NARUMON, MS. ORNRAMPHA
JITRADA, JIRAPHAT, THEERARUTH, IRIN

10
00:02:08,180 --> 00:02:10,140
Why does it say ‘Theeraruth’?

11
00:02:10,470 --> 00:02:12,220
Isn’t his name Atiwitch?

12
00:02:12,600 --> 00:02:15,550
You knew Ruth before, Ji?

13
00:02:15,770 --> 00:02:17,640
How come you never told me that?

14
00:02:18,710 --> 00:02:20,310
How could someone like Ji remember that?

15
00:02:20,670 --> 00:02:24,360
He doesn’t even remember what he ate yesterday.

16
00:02:25,330 --> 00:02:26,670
But don’t forget, Jean.

17
00:02:26,960 --> 00:02:28,590
After what happened,

18
00:02:28,620 --> 00:02:31,620
we agreed that if Ji couldn’t remember anything,

19
00:02:31,660 --> 00:02:32,750
we would let it go

20
00:02:33,080 --> 00:02:34,420
and never mention it again.

21
00:02:36,260 --> 00:02:38,700
Ma’am, I think I smell something burning.

22
00:02:40,580 --> 00:02:42,310
Oh, no! I left the fish in the pan!

23
00:02:46,410 --> 00:02:49,160
Enough about me. Do you even remember what happened?

24
00:02:49,190 --> 00:02:50,620
I’m not like you.

25
00:02:51,210 --> 00:02:55,870
Besides, do you know that even though Mom and Ms. Orn don’t see each other,

26
00:02:55,890 --> 00:02:57,090
they always talk on the phone?

27
00:02:57,840 --> 00:02:59,400
Why has nobody ever told me about this?

28
00:02:59,770 --> 00:03:01,800
It was a long time ago.

29
00:03:02,550 --> 00:03:04,440
You were in Grade 1.

30
00:03:04,860 --> 00:03:06,300
What’s the point of telling you?

31
00:03:07,330 --> 00:03:10,940
How did our family and their family
know each other then?

32
00:03:11,450 --> 00:03:12,450
It’s a long story.

33
00:03:18,960 --> 00:03:20,810
You can unload these things from the truck.

34
00:03:20,840 --> 00:03:22,420
- Yes, ma’am.
- Please be careful.

35
00:03:22,740 --> 00:03:23,740
- Mom.
- Hmm?

36
00:03:23,880 --> 00:03:24,930
Where’s Papa?

37
00:03:25,160 --> 00:03:27,120
Papa and Khun have work to do.

38
00:03:27,590 --> 00:03:29,750
The three of us have to stay here
by ourselves for now.

39
00:03:30,130 --> 00:03:31,820
Do you want to see Papa, Ruth?

40
00:03:31,860 --> 00:03:32,960
I can take you to see him.

41
00:03:35,830 --> 00:03:37,620
(Don’t run, Ji. You’ll fall.)

42
00:03:37,650 --> 00:03:38,960
I won’t, Mom.

43
00:03:46,550 --> 00:03:47,550
Who’s that?

44
00:03:50,590 --> 00:03:51,180
Luke?

45
00:03:51,540 --> 00:03:52,540
Ruth.

46
00:03:52,600 --> 00:03:53,600
Ruke?

47
00:03:54,160 --> 00:03:54,710
Ruth.

48
00:03:54,940 --> 00:03:56,170
Ugh, I don’t like it.

49
00:03:56,480 --> 00:03:57,440
It’s hard to pronounce.

50
00:03:57,460 --> 00:04:00,080
Ruth’s first name is Theeraruth.

51
00:04:00,380 --> 00:04:02,080
You can call him Tee instead.

52
00:04:02,490 --> 00:04:04,060
Okay, that’s better.

53
00:04:04,550 --> 00:04:05,560
What’s up, Tee?

54
00:04:12,510 --> 00:04:13,510
Ji.

55
00:04:13,980 --> 00:04:15,166
You can’t leave the school grounds.

56
00:04:15,190 --> 00:04:16,870
We have ten minutes before the van leaves.

57
00:04:16,900 --> 00:04:17,900
Let’s go grab a bite.

58
00:04:20,520 --> 00:04:22,650
(My mama says candy is bad.)

59
00:04:22,680 --> 00:04:23,680
(It causes cavities.)

60
00:04:23,900 --> 00:04:24,986
This is fishing monkey candy.

61
00:04:25,010 --> 00:04:26,720
My mom says eating fish makes you smart.

62
00:04:34,000 --> 00:04:36,000
Keep trying. You’ll get the hang of it.

63
00:04:36,020 --> 00:04:37,200
- (Honey.)
- Yeah?

64
00:04:37,230 --> 00:04:38,800
(Can you bring out another table?)

65
00:04:40,320 --> 00:04:41,320
That’s enough.

66
00:04:41,700 --> 00:04:42,940
It’s okay if you can’t ride it.

67
00:04:43,400 --> 00:04:44,400
Don’t worry.

68
00:04:45,460 --> 00:04:46,460
(Today...)

69
00:04:47,530 --> 00:04:49,610
(I’ll take you for a ride around the block.)

70
00:04:50,550 --> 00:04:52,180
(Because you’ve been a good boy.)

71
00:04:54,020 --> 00:04:55,020
(You’re the best)

72
00:04:59,820 --> 00:05:03,060
(Honey, have you got everything?
(I’m almost ready.)

73
00:05:03,230 --> 00:05:06,040
(Hey, I’m ready. Here.)

74
00:05:06,060 --> 00:05:07,750
We’re going to the beach, kids.

75
00:05:08,090 --> 00:05:09,520
Yay!

76
00:05:09,560 --> 00:05:11,660
Okay, let’s go. We’re all set.

77
00:05:43,230 --> 00:05:45,960
Ji, let’s go home. This place is creepy.

78
00:05:46,280 --> 00:05:47,520
Not at all.

79
00:06:07,980 --> 00:06:09,390
Tee, wake up!

80
00:06:15,380 --> 00:06:17,010
Use this. Don’t drop it.

81
00:06:17,720 --> 00:06:19,370
Hold my hand. Don’t ever let go.

82
00:06:19,990 --> 00:06:20,990
1...

83
00:06:21,540 --> 00:06:22,540
2...

84
00:06:23,060 --> 00:06:24,060
3.

85
00:06:24,460 --> 00:06:25,100
Please!

86
00:06:25,320 --> 00:06:26,320
Keep off!

87
00:06:30,270 --> 00:06:31,290
Ruth! Ruth!

88
00:06:31,980 --> 00:06:32,980
Excuse me.

89
00:06:33,490 --> 00:06:34,370
- Ruth! Ruth!
- Ji!

90
00:06:34,400 --> 00:06:35,400
Mom!

91
00:06:40,910 --> 00:06:42,720
- (Are you okay?)
- (Ji!)

92
00:06:43,100 --> 00:06:44,100
Ji!

93
00:06:44,140 --> 00:06:44,650
Ji

94
00:06:44,900 --> 00:06:45,710
Ji. Baby!

95
00:06:45,730 --> 00:06:46,730
- Ji!
- Ji!

96
00:06:47,600 --> 00:06:48,600
- Are you alright?
- Ji!

97
00:07:16,110 --> 00:07:16,480
Ruth!

98
00:07:16,510 --> 00:07:17,980
Ruth! Ruth! Ruth! Ruth!

99
00:07:18,020 --> 00:07:20,010
Sir! Sir! We need help here!

100
00:07:20,180 --> 00:07:21,680
Ruth! Ruth! Baby!

101
00:07:21,710 --> 00:07:22,840
Ruth! Ruth!

102
00:07:23,560 --> 00:07:24,560
Please help!

103
00:07:34,420 --> 00:07:35,420
Ruth’s awake.

104
00:07:36,360 --> 00:07:38,220
Ruth, how are you?

105
00:07:40,610 --> 00:07:42,220
Easy, easy. You’re safe now.

106
00:07:48,420 --> 00:07:49,420
Mom...

107
00:07:49,830 --> 00:07:50,510
Where’s Ji?

108
00:07:50,820 --> 00:07:53,060
Why would you want to see the one
who put you in danger?

109
00:07:54,200 --> 00:07:55,200
Honey.

110
00:07:57,620 --> 00:07:59,340
Ji is okay now.

111
00:07:59,660 --> 00:08:01,340
But he needs to rest, okay?

112
00:08:01,360 --> 00:08:02,550
We’ll visit him later.

113
00:08:03,820 --> 00:08:06,520
Ruth, after you’re released from the hospital,

114
00:08:06,910 --> 00:08:08,310
let’s move back to our house, okay?

115
00:08:10,310 --> 00:08:12,870
You’ll get to go to the same school as Tawan,

116
00:08:12,890 --> 00:08:13,980
Pim, and Lita again.

117
00:08:14,460 --> 00:08:15,460
Are you glad, honey?

118
00:08:18,280 --> 00:08:22,640
But… if you don’t want to move back, you don’t have to.

119
00:08:22,660 --> 00:08:23,780
Whatever you want.

120
00:08:24,310 --> 00:08:25,760
What about Papa?

121
00:08:26,260 --> 00:08:29,470
Papa… will have to go back and forth

122
00:08:29,500 --> 00:08:31,470
because it’s far from where he works.

123
00:08:33,100 --> 00:08:34,470
I want to move back to our house.

124
00:08:34,500 --> 00:08:35,380
I’m glad, Mom.

125
00:08:35,420 --> 00:08:37,080
Mmm, okay.

126
00:08:41,260 --> 00:08:43,880
You can always come back here.

127
00:08:44,130 --> 00:08:45,620
Thank you so much, Mon.

128
00:08:45,980 --> 00:08:48,900
Both of you were always there for us.

129
00:08:49,300 --> 00:08:50,886
Lately, there have been nothing but bad rumors.

130
00:08:50,910 --> 00:08:53,590
I’m thinking of taking Ruth to change
his name to ward off bad luck.

131
00:08:53,670 --> 00:08:54,540
Good luck.

132
00:08:54,560 --> 00:08:56,540
I’ll miss you guys.

133
00:08:57,990 --> 00:09:01,440
(From that day on, I completely forgot about everything.)

134
00:09:02,420 --> 00:09:04,420
(The memories of Theeraruth)

135
00:09:05,050 --> 00:09:08,260
(were buried beneath a pile of forgotten old CDs.)

136
00:09:08,280 --> 00:09:10,090
That’s what happened.

137
00:09:12,090 --> 00:09:13,200
Did I forget anything?

138
00:09:14,230 --> 00:09:15,500
That’s pretty much it.

139
00:09:16,120 --> 00:09:17,320
After that incident,

140
00:09:17,600 --> 00:09:20,320
their family transferred their son back to
his former private school.

141
00:09:20,770 --> 00:09:24,580
I’m surprised Ruth and Ji have become
close again.

142
00:09:26,190 --> 00:09:27,190
Hey.

143
00:09:27,690 --> 00:09:29,320
Hey, Kong. Hey, Kong.

144
00:09:31,170 --> 00:09:32,170
Wake up.

145
00:09:32,220 --> 00:09:33,300
They’ve finished the story.

146
00:09:33,900 --> 00:09:37,890
Ty's Songkran ordeal was more entertaining.

147
00:09:38,760 --> 00:09:41,500
Sorry my life is so uneventful.

148
00:09:42,830 --> 00:09:45,740
It might sound trivial now,

149
00:09:46,120 --> 00:09:48,420
but I was really shocked back then.

150
00:09:48,450 --> 00:09:51,910
I was so shocked I didn't know what to do.

151
00:09:52,910 --> 00:09:55,060
It’s good you didn’t remember it back then.

152
00:09:57,140 --> 00:09:58,740
Mom, let me help.

153
00:09:59,260 --> 00:10:00,440
I’ll help, too.

154
00:10:07,250 --> 00:10:08,250
Ji.

155
00:10:08,560 --> 00:10:10,620
Honestly, the story of you and your friend Ruth

156
00:10:10,660 --> 00:10:12,460
is more entertaining than the dramas I watch.

157
00:10:12,820 --> 00:10:13,900
What are you talking about?

158
00:10:14,640 --> 00:10:15,750
Think about it.

159
00:10:16,460 --> 00:10:17,870
You two grew up together.

160
00:10:18,310 --> 00:10:19,880
Your parents are close.

161
00:10:19,920 --> 00:10:21,540
You used to be neighbors.

162
00:10:21,720 --> 00:10:23,706
You’ve escaped a life-and-death situation together.

163
00:10:23,730 --> 00:10:25,640
And you get to see each other again.

164
00:10:27,430 --> 00:10:29,210
This is straight out of a romantic drama.

165
00:10:30,310 --> 00:10:31,310
It’s meant to be.

166
00:10:31,600 --> 00:10:32,800
It’s destiny.

167
00:10:34,950 --> 00:10:36,600
- Let’s go!
- Tyler!

168
00:10:37,220 --> 00:10:39,090
(Kids, dinner’s ready.)

169
00:10:39,120 --> 00:10:40,690
Okay, we’re coming.

170
00:10:54,640 --> 00:10:56,980
Oh, have your friends left?

171
00:10:57,700 --> 00:10:58,700
Yes.

172
00:11:00,420 --> 00:11:01,520
Go take a shower, then?

173
00:11:01,540 --> 00:11:02,680
Why are you sitting here?

174
00:11:03,600 --> 00:11:06,180
Are you preparing the ingredients for tomorrow?

175
00:11:06,810 --> 00:11:08,910
Yes, but you don’t have to help me.

176
00:11:08,940 --> 00:11:10,330
I’m almost done.

177
00:11:10,350 --> 00:11:12,120
I’ll continue tomorrow.

178
00:11:14,220 --> 00:11:15,220
Well...

179
00:11:17,420 --> 00:11:19,020
If you don’t mind,

180
00:11:19,650 --> 00:11:22,000
can I ask you to do something tomorrow?

181
00:11:37,400 --> 00:11:40,520
(Maybe him looking at the sky that day)

182
00:11:40,780 --> 00:11:42,100
(was a sign of something.)

183
00:11:44,500 --> 00:11:45,880
(But I was too afraid to ask him.)

184
00:11:51,880 --> 00:11:52,420
Wow.

185
00:11:52,700 --> 00:11:55,030
Looks so tasty. Where did you buy it?

186
00:11:55,340 --> 00:11:56,360
My friend’s mom’s place.

187
00:11:56,980 --> 00:12:01,340
Oh. Have you guys decided which school
you’re attending?

188
00:12:01,680 --> 00:12:02,680
Not yet.

189
00:12:02,770 --> 00:12:05,880
Then… why don’t we go to the same school?

190
00:12:06,150 --> 00:12:08,520
But there’s an entrance exam, right?

191
00:12:08,960 --> 00:12:09,960
Yeah.

192
00:12:10,760 --> 00:12:12,240
But don’t worry.

193
00:12:12,430 --> 00:12:14,940
It’s not a popular school.

194
00:12:14,980 --> 00:12:16,840
You don’t need to study that hard.

195
00:12:16,880 --> 00:12:21,520
Plus, there’s an egg yolk ice-cream shop nearby.

196
00:12:21,560 --> 00:12:23,500
Let’s go to this school, then.

197
00:12:24,890 --> 00:12:25,890
Wanna join us?

198
00:12:27,000 --> 00:12:28,000
Why not?

199
00:12:30,300 --> 00:12:31,300
(Eventually, )

200
00:12:31,720 --> 00:12:34,080
(I got a chance to be back in his world again.)

201
00:12:52,550 --> 00:12:54,600
How can you put up with that old mean teacher?

202
00:12:54,930 --> 00:12:56,290
He’s the only one

203
00:12:56,440 --> 00:12:59,900
who can convince Ms. Suda to meet us halfway.

204
00:13:00,460 --> 00:13:01,900
She just agreed to share her notes with us,

205
00:13:01,920 --> 00:13:02,926
but she’d probably still be so biased

206
00:13:02,950 --> 00:13:04,870
that students would end up skipping class again.

207
00:13:06,410 --> 00:13:08,060
There are some free seats over there.

208
00:13:08,100 --> 00:13:10,140
- Let’s ask him if we can have a seat.
- Yeah.

209
00:13:10,490 --> 00:13:11,900
I think he’d rather be alone.

210
00:13:12,510 --> 00:13:14,040
Let’s sit somewhere else.

211
00:13:14,580 --> 00:13:16,160
Mmm, okay.

212
00:13:16,740 --> 00:13:18,500
Oh, he’s leaving.

213
00:13:18,540 --> 00:13:19,540
Come on.

214
00:13:27,850 --> 00:13:31,740
(If I had turned around and gotten to know
him again that day, )

215
00:13:34,190 --> 00:13:35,716
(would things have turned out differently?)

216
00:13:35,740 --> 00:13:39,860
(would things have turned out differently?)
JIRAPHAT JAROENWONG
BORN: 31 OCTOBER 1993, DIED: 4 MARCH 2023

217
00:13:50,140 --> 00:13:53,000
STUDENT COUNCIL, NAWINA SCHOOL
ATIWITCH RATTANAWATTHANA,
CLASS PRESIDENT

218
00:13:54,020 --> 00:13:55,490
Oh, hi.

219
00:13:57,180 --> 00:13:58,180
Hi.

220
00:14:00,540 --> 00:14:02,360
Have you eaten?

221
00:14:02,710 --> 00:14:03,710
I have.

222
00:14:11,230 --> 00:14:12,230
Ruth.

223
00:14:13,790 --> 00:14:14,790
Hmm?

224
00:14:16,980 --> 00:14:18,380
I know the truth.

225
00:14:19,470 --> 00:14:20,470
The truth?

226
00:14:22,390 --> 00:14:23,390
Yes.

227
00:14:29,420 --> 00:14:30,420
You...

228
00:14:31,980 --> 00:14:33,430
You know everything?

229
00:14:34,040 --> 00:14:35,040
Yes.

230
00:14:35,720 --> 00:14:36,880
Everything.

231
00:14:38,040 --> 00:14:40,100
(Ji knows that I came back in time?)

232
00:14:41,750 --> 00:14:42,750
Does this mean…

233
00:14:44,360 --> 00:14:45,580
You know that…

234
00:14:46,750 --> 00:14:48,310
If I hadn’t figured it out myself,

235
00:14:49,200 --> 00:14:50,940
you wouldn’t have told me anyway?

236
00:14:52,790 --> 00:14:55,830
I thought you were living your best life.

237
00:14:56,700 --> 00:14:59,680
So I didn’t want to remind you of those sad memories.

238
00:15:00,080 --> 00:15:01,870
Wait a second. What sad memories?

239
00:15:01,900 --> 00:15:03,170
What’s sad about this?

240
00:15:06,670 --> 00:15:09,050
Here. Thai desserts by Ms. Narumon.

241
00:15:09,070 --> 00:15:10,740
A 100-year-old family recipe.

242
00:15:12,060 --> 00:15:15,440
But you have to come to my house to enjoy
the hot cocoa.

243
00:15:16,230 --> 00:15:17,580
For today, just take these.

244
00:15:25,530 --> 00:15:28,410
This is ‘the truth’ you were talking about?

245
00:15:28,860 --> 00:15:31,880
That’s right, Theeraruth.

246
00:15:43,850 --> 00:15:44,850
You like them?

247
00:15:45,500 --> 00:15:46,500
Want some?

248
00:15:52,710 --> 00:15:53,710
Aren’t you mad?

249
00:15:55,140 --> 00:15:56,766
Even after my mom and Jean told me every detail,

250
00:15:56,790 --> 00:15:58,510
I couldn’t remember a thing.

251
00:15:58,970 --> 00:16:00,150
How can I be mad at you?

252
00:16:02,150 --> 00:16:03,890
I told you not to worry about it.

253
00:16:04,240 --> 00:16:06,230
You never came to me and said hi.

254
00:16:06,280 --> 00:16:07,790
And I forgot all about us.

255
00:16:07,820 --> 00:16:08,820
Let’s call it even.

256
00:16:13,340 --> 00:16:14,340
That’s fair, right?

257
00:16:15,440 --> 00:16:17,890
- Eat it up. You haven’t tried this.
- Let’s share.

258
00:16:29,020 --> 00:16:33,430
THURSDAY, 16 SEPTEMBER 2010

259
00:16:36,870 --> 00:16:38,220
Should I let them know

260
00:16:38,250 --> 00:16:40,360
that they’re not alone in this room?

261
00:16:41,030 --> 00:16:42,030
Do you want to?

262
00:16:43,260 --> 00:16:44,260
Who would?

263
00:16:47,820 --> 00:16:51,640
These are the final exam guidelines.
FRIDAY, 17 SEPTEMBER 2010

264
00:16:51,670 --> 00:16:53,796
Good luck with your exams, everyone.
BHUJANGAPRAYATA CHANDA

265
00:16:53,820 --> 00:16:56,040
Attention, students.

266
00:16:56,330 --> 00:16:58,270
- Thank you, ma’am.
- Thank you.

267
00:17:01,700 --> 00:17:03,920
The final exams are coming up before we know it.

268
00:17:04,110 --> 00:17:06,160
Besides, we have to prepare for Sports Day.

269
00:17:06,190 --> 00:17:07,040
Ugh.

270
00:17:07,080 --> 00:17:10,000
- Being in Grade 11 is so exhausting.
- Facts.

271
00:17:10,360 --> 00:17:12,210
How are we supposed to find time to study?

272
00:17:12,640 --> 00:17:13,760
Why don’t we study together?

273
00:17:18,210 --> 00:17:20,210
Ruth said he’d tutor us.

274
00:17:20,800 --> 00:17:21,800
Ugh.

275
00:17:21,840 --> 00:17:22,840
Ruth again.

276
00:17:23,080 --> 00:17:24,730
All you talk about is Ruth.

277
00:17:25,840 --> 00:17:27,420
- Hey, are you blushing?
- What?

278
00:17:27,460 --> 00:17:29,020
Gotcha.

279
00:17:29,050 --> 00:17:29,970
- Gotcha.
- Hey, it’s not that.

280
00:17:30,000 --> 00:17:31,360
- Your ears are red.
- They’re not.

281
00:17:46,060 --> 00:17:47,100
Why are you staring at me?

282
00:17:48,680 --> 00:17:49,680
Just want to look at you?

283
00:17:52,440 --> 00:17:53,720
I’ll charge you.

284
00:17:55,390 --> 00:17:56,400
I can pay.

285
00:18:03,130 --> 00:18:07,000
Now that my parents know we’re friends again,

286
00:18:08,000 --> 00:18:09,880
they want you to come over for dinner.

287
00:18:11,940 --> 00:18:13,160
Don’t worry.

288
00:18:13,400 --> 00:18:15,160
My mom and dad like you.

289
00:18:16,580 --> 00:18:17,890
- They do?
- Yeah.

290
00:18:18,720 --> 00:18:19,720
Besides,

291
00:18:20,240 --> 00:18:21,630
I’ll be right there with you.

292
00:18:27,780 --> 00:18:29,340
- Okay then.
- Really?

293
00:18:29,770 --> 00:18:31,690
Come over after the exam then.

294
00:18:31,920 --> 00:18:33,320
Kongpob and Tyler are coming, too.

295
00:18:33,600 --> 00:18:35,890
In case someone gets nervous.

296
00:18:43,220 --> 00:18:44,220
Finish your homework.

297
00:18:53,310 --> 00:18:55,070
Stop staring. Finish it.

298
00:18:59,880 --> 00:19:02,420
FINAL EXAM
FRIDAY, 24 SEPTEMBER 2010

299
00:19:15,880 --> 00:19:17,880
School’s over!

300
00:19:18,020 --> 00:19:18,770
Wooo!
Hey.

301
00:19:19,780 --> 00:19:22,130
You still have to come to Sports Day practice.

302
00:19:22,290 --> 00:19:25,230
If you don't show up, I'll charge you
extra next semester.

303
00:19:25,410 --> 00:19:26,360
You wouldn't dare.

304
00:19:26,390 --> 00:19:27,580
Why wouldn't I?

305
00:19:27,660 --> 00:19:28,660
Okay, fine.

306
00:19:28,680 --> 00:19:30,370
- Scary.
- Don’t play with me.

307
00:19:32,910 --> 00:19:34,370
- Yes, I’m done.
- You’re done?

308
00:19:34,400 --> 00:19:35,720
Yeah, finally.

309
00:19:35,750 --> 00:19:37,520
(This semester went by so fast.)

310
00:19:37,940 --> 00:19:41,470
(Looking back, I've made so many
wonderful memories)

311
00:19:41,510 --> 00:19:43,210
(with my friends in Class 7.)

312
00:19:44,600 --> 00:19:46,100
Move. Get out of my way.

313
00:19:46,130 --> 00:19:47,500
I’ll finish cleaning up so I can go home.

314
00:19:47,520 --> 00:19:48,820
Move it. Move it.

315
00:19:48,850 --> 00:19:50,450
Move it. Move it. Move it.

316
00:19:50,480 --> 00:19:52,360
Move it. I told you to move it.

317
00:19:52,380 --> 00:19:53,450
Out of my way.

318
00:19:54,170 --> 00:19:55,670
- What?
- You think you’re the main character?

319
00:19:55,690 --> 00:19:57,260
Why are you standing here

320
00:19:57,300 --> 00:19:59,190
instead of helping me clean up so we can leave?

321
00:19:59,220 --> 00:20:00,420
- Whose duty is this?
- Mine.

322
00:20:01,140 --> 00:20:02,910
Ji, Kong just called.

323
00:20:02,930 --> 00:20:04,490
He’s waiting for us in front of school.

324
00:20:04,520 --> 00:20:05,100
Hold on a sec.

325
00:20:05,470 --> 00:20:06,160
Yeah, hold on.

326
00:20:06,190 --> 00:20:07,900
Help me clean up.

327
00:20:09,010 --> 00:20:10,040
- Oh, wow.
- Oh.

328
00:20:11,750 --> 00:20:13,120
Last time you ditched me,

329
00:20:13,570 --> 00:20:15,010
and I had to clean up all by myself.

330
00:20:15,850 --> 00:20:16,990
Now it’s your turn.

331
00:20:17,020 --> 00:20:19,120
See you next semester, Gun Gun, my best friend.

332
00:20:19,980 --> 00:20:21,180
Let’s go, Tyler.

333
00:20:21,220 --> 00:20:23,000
- See you, man.
- See you.

334
00:20:23,040 --> 00:20:24,450
How can you do this to me?

335
00:20:25,110 --> 00:20:26,930
- Hey, you finish this. I’m done.
- Hey.

336
00:20:29,960 --> 00:20:32,160
Wow!

337
00:20:32,180 --> 00:20:33,520
If you don’t mind…

338
00:20:33,570 --> 00:20:34,880
I want some meat.

339
00:20:36,130 --> 00:20:37,910
Hot, hot, hot.

340
00:20:38,360 --> 00:20:39,360
Careful.

341
00:20:39,440 --> 00:20:42,260
Crab stick, Ty’s favorite.

342
00:20:42,300 --> 00:20:43,100
Thank you.

343
00:20:43,130 --> 00:20:45,100
- And Kong’s favorite.
- Thank you.

344
00:20:46,130 --> 00:20:48,130
I’ll go get more.

345
00:20:49,440 --> 00:20:51,800
There, there, Ji.

346
00:20:51,830 --> 00:20:52,830
Here.

347
00:20:53,330 --> 00:20:54,330
Thank you.

348
00:20:55,910 --> 00:20:56,910
But I didn’t ask.

349
00:20:57,900 --> 00:20:59,120
If you don’t want it…

350
00:20:59,340 --> 00:21:00,700
- Umm, take it.
- Let me have some.

351
00:21:00,840 --> 00:21:02,540
Umm, take it. Hey, that’s my crab stick.

352
00:21:02,570 --> 00:21:03,756
- I know what it is.
- My favorite.

353
00:21:03,780 --> 00:21:06,700
Hey, I thought Ruth was coming, too.

354
00:21:06,810 --> 00:21:07,970
Why isn’t he here?

355
00:21:08,190 --> 00:21:10,180
Ruth has a meeting at school.

356
00:21:10,220 --> 00:21:11,100
He’ll be here soon.

357
00:21:11,140 --> 00:21:13,520
Oh, he’s the class president, right?

358
00:21:14,600 --> 00:21:16,380
Unlike you, he has work to do.

359
00:21:16,410 --> 00:21:17,920
Zip it.

360
00:21:19,180 --> 00:21:21,070
Hey, Ji. Ruth’s here. Ruth’s here.

361
00:21:22,320 --> 00:21:23,660
I think that’s my dad.

362
00:21:23,900 --> 00:21:25,360
Maybe Ruth’s not coming.

363
00:21:25,580 --> 00:21:26,580
Are you two really close?

364
00:21:27,610 --> 00:21:29,250
Well… we’re pretty close.

365
00:21:30,670 --> 00:21:31,670
It’s true, Jean.

366
00:21:31,760 --> 00:21:33,980
Ji and Ruth are one step closer than the rest of us.

367
00:21:34,740 --> 00:21:38,590
Hmm, you guys have a way of measuring
how close you are?

368
00:21:38,640 --> 00:21:39,500
Yeah.

369
00:21:39,550 --> 00:21:41,890
Ji doesn’t see Ruth as just a friend.

370
00:21:43,220 --> 00:21:43,930
- Ji...
- Ahem!

371
00:21:43,960 --> 00:21:44,960
Tyler.

372
00:21:46,470 --> 00:21:48,020
I mean… Uh…

373
00:21:48,390 --> 00:21:50,500
Ji has known Ruth since they were kids.

374
00:21:50,530 --> 00:21:52,040
So they are really close.

375
00:21:52,080 --> 00:21:53,330
Yeah, close friends.

376
00:21:53,370 --> 00:21:54,910
- Right.
- Right, Ji?

377
00:21:55,840 --> 00:21:57,220
Hey, Ruth’s here, Ji.

378
00:21:57,700 --> 00:21:58,700
Tyler.

379
00:22:01,680 --> 00:22:02,400
- Good evening.
- Good evening.

380
00:22:02,440 --> 00:22:04,540
Oh, good evening, kids.

381
00:22:07,320 --> 00:22:08,320
Ji.

382
00:22:09,270 --> 00:22:10,740
When I was at the gate,

383
00:22:10,780 --> 00:22:13,110
I saw someone lurking around outside.

384
00:22:13,310 --> 00:22:14,840
I thought it was a burglar.

385
00:22:14,890 --> 00:22:16,616
But then I got a closer look and he resembled

386
00:22:16,640 --> 00:22:17,600
Diruth as a teenager.

387
00:22:17,630 --> 00:22:18,840
That’s when I figured it out.

388
00:22:19,300 --> 00:22:20,300
Oh, Ruth.

389
00:22:20,480 --> 00:22:21,576
- Good evening, ma’am.
- Honey.

390
00:22:21,600 --> 00:22:23,200
I haven’t seen you for ages.

391
00:22:23,460 --> 00:22:24,760
You’re taller than Ji now.

392
00:22:25,000 --> 00:22:26,100
How are you doing?

393
00:22:26,370 --> 00:22:27,370
I’m great, ma’am.

394
00:22:27,660 --> 00:22:29,620
My mom and dad wanted me to give you this.

395
00:22:29,660 --> 00:22:30,660
Wow.

396
00:22:30,910 --> 00:22:32,750
How nice of Ms. Orn.

397
00:22:32,780 --> 00:22:34,970
- But I can’t...
- Take it, honey.

398
00:22:35,020 --> 00:22:37,860
Diruth isn't someone who often spends
money on us.

399
00:22:37,900 --> 00:22:40,360
I’ll make them some desserts sometime.

400
00:22:40,390 --> 00:22:41,986
- Thank you, ma’am.
- Come on. Let’s eat.

401
00:22:42,010 --> 00:22:43,320
Go on. Let’s have dinner.

402
00:22:43,370 --> 00:22:44,280
Have a seat, son.

403
00:22:44,310 --> 00:22:45,310
- Here?
- Have a seat.

404
00:22:52,340 --> 00:22:53,920
- Thank you.
- This is delicious.

405
00:22:54,270 --> 00:22:56,510
- Can I have more crab sticks, please?
- Can I have some?

406
00:22:57,560 --> 00:22:59,140
- You get one each.
- Thank you.

407
00:23:04,440 --> 00:23:06,760
- Can I eat this now?
- You’ll see.

408
00:23:06,790 --> 00:23:08,780
- Sorry, sorry.
- Dad.

409
00:23:08,800 --> 00:23:10,060
I didn’t mean to.

410
00:23:12,460 --> 00:23:13,460
Thank you.

411
00:23:16,160 --> 00:23:17,520
There’s enough for everyone, kids.

412
00:23:34,140 --> 00:23:35,200
What the hell?

413
00:23:37,440 --> 00:23:39,440
I let Mhee attack me so many times

414
00:23:39,940 --> 00:23:40,980
before he let me hold him.

415
00:23:42,760 --> 00:23:44,040
I already told you, Ji,

416
00:23:44,540 --> 00:23:46,250
that Ruth is the most dangerous one.

417
00:23:47,360 --> 00:23:48,300
He brought gifts for your family.

418
00:23:48,330 --> 00:23:49,510
So when you visit his house,

419
00:23:49,540 --> 00:23:50,716
you should do the same, right?

420
00:23:50,740 --> 00:23:51,740
I think so.

421
00:23:52,580 --> 00:23:53,580
Now hold on.

422
00:23:53,860 --> 00:23:55,390
Why do I have to go to Ruth’s house?

423
00:23:55,430 --> 00:23:57,670
- You’ll have to go there eventually, right?
- Umm, yeah.

424
00:24:10,300 --> 00:24:11,340
Did I say something wrong?

425
00:24:11,460 --> 00:24:12,460
You didn’t.

426
00:24:13,070 --> 00:24:14,070
Let’s eat.

427
00:24:15,060 --> 00:24:16,320
It’s just us now.

428
00:24:21,440 --> 00:24:22,840
You must have done something right.

429
00:24:22,970 --> 00:24:24,690
You got Mhee to sit on your lap.

430
00:24:25,280 --> 00:24:25,880
Really?

431
00:24:26,220 --> 00:24:27,220
Yeah.

432
00:24:29,640 --> 00:24:31,240
Did I do well?

433
00:24:35,290 --> 00:24:36,660
I never thought someone like you

434
00:24:36,690 --> 00:24:37,890
would care what I think.

435
00:24:40,200 --> 00:24:43,260
It didn’t take long for you to become my parents’ favorite.

436
00:24:44,050 --> 00:24:45,850
Since they found out we’d become close again,

437
00:24:46,120 --> 00:24:47,456
they couldn’t stop asking me about you.

438
00:24:47,480 --> 00:24:49,000
There’s no way they wouldn’t like you.

439
00:24:50,160 --> 00:24:51,200
But back then...

440
00:24:53,870 --> 00:24:55,176
If I hadn't let go of your hand...

441
00:24:55,200 --> 00:24:57,600
Would you have held my hand and followed me,

442
00:24:57,640 --> 00:24:59,116
leaving your own mother standing there,

443
00:24:59,140 --> 00:25:00,310
crying out for her son?

444
00:25:00,600 --> 00:25:02,640
I'd have been really mad at you if you'd done that.

445
00:25:05,810 --> 00:25:09,490
Besides... maybe I only befriended you back then

446
00:25:10,040 --> 00:25:11,996
because I was jealous of how rich your family was.

447
00:25:12,020 --> 00:25:13,050
Who knows?

448
00:25:23,790 --> 00:25:24,910
Are you free tomorrow?

449
00:25:26,820 --> 00:25:27,820
I think so.

450
00:25:28,020 --> 00:25:30,120
I guess I’ll just be lying around in bed.

451
00:25:30,450 --> 00:25:31,460
Then…

452
00:25:32,510 --> 00:25:33,630
Will you go out with me?

453
00:25:34,620 --> 00:25:36,680
Sure. Where and when?

454
00:25:36,910 --> 00:25:38,030
I’ll invite the others, too.

455
00:25:39,780 --> 00:25:40,980
Uh...

456
00:25:41,010 --> 00:25:42,140
You’ve invited them?

457
00:25:44,460 --> 00:25:45,460
I haven’t.

458
00:25:46,960 --> 00:25:47,960
Just you.

459
00:25:52,800 --> 00:25:54,310
I just want to go with you.

460
00:25:58,450 --> 00:26:00,380
Okay, just us two.

461
00:26:06,320 --> 00:26:10,580
- Meow, meow, meow, meow.
- Meow, meow, meow, meow.

462
00:26:10,640 --> 00:26:11,900
Meow.

463
00:26:11,940 --> 00:26:13,550
Mhee, come out, Mhee.

464
00:26:13,570 --> 00:26:14,400
Mhee. Mhee.

465
00:26:14,440 --> 00:26:16,400
- Mhee, meow, meow.
- Meow, meow, meow.

466
00:26:16,980 --> 00:26:19,740
- Meow, meow.
- Meow, meow.

467
00:26:19,780 --> 00:26:21,270
Hey, you scared him.

468
00:26:21,300 --> 00:26:22,560
- Honey.
- Hmm?

469
00:26:22,970 --> 00:26:25,070
- Are Ji’s friends all there?
- Meow.

470
00:26:25,100 --> 00:26:27,510
- Meow.
- Meow.

471
00:26:35,940 --> 00:26:36,940
You’re hungry?

472
00:26:37,580 --> 00:26:39,050
No, I’ve eaten at home.

473
00:26:40,290 --> 00:26:42,740
Let’s walk around until you get hungry then.

474
00:26:48,280 --> 00:26:49,280
You wanna go in there?

475
00:26:50,740 --> 00:26:51,740
Nah.

476
00:26:53,360 --> 00:26:54,360
Let’s do it.

477
00:27:03,240 --> 00:27:04,610
We don’t have to.

478
00:27:06,650 --> 00:27:07,650
Just do it.

479
00:27:08,270 --> 00:27:09,910
We might not get another chance tomorrow.

480
00:27:10,250 --> 00:27:11,080
Why would you say that?

481
00:27:11,110 --> 00:27:12,110
Who knows?

482
00:27:12,440 --> 00:27:13,740
It might come back someday.

483
00:27:14,300 --> 00:27:15,740
Just like vintage items.

484
00:27:16,430 --> 00:27:17,880
They always come back around.

485
00:27:19,740 --> 00:27:22,140
The only thing that makes a comeback
is sticker photo booths,

486
00:27:22,570 --> 00:27:23,570
not us.

487
00:27:34,800 --> 00:27:35,800
Come closer.

488
00:27:39,140 --> 00:27:40,660
Your head is almost out of the frame.

489
00:27:41,440 --> 00:27:42,440
Move in.

490
00:27:44,300 --> 00:27:45,300
Ready?

491
00:28:15,650 --> 00:28:16,650
- Let me see.
- Hey!

492
00:28:16,880 --> 00:28:17,550
No!

493
00:28:17,580 --> 00:28:18,760
The picture is blurry.

494
00:28:19,820 --> 00:28:21,020
Want to take another one?

495
00:28:21,050 --> 00:28:22,050
Hey, no!

496
00:28:25,250 --> 00:28:26,330
Wanna get something to eat?

497
00:28:26,590 --> 00:28:27,590
Sure.

498
00:28:28,540 --> 00:28:29,540
What do you wanna eat?

499
00:28:30,370 --> 00:28:31,560
Uh...

500
00:28:32,160 --> 00:28:33,160
Anything.

501
00:28:33,473 --> 00:28:35,340
How about noodles?

502
00:28:36,060 --> 00:28:37,246
No, I don’t want that.

503
00:28:38,020 --> 00:28:39,953
But you always have noodles at school.

504
00:28:39,973 --> 00:28:42,220
The food stalls at school mostly sell spicy food,

505
00:28:43,073 --> 00:28:44,260
fried food, and greasy food.

506
00:28:44,293 --> 00:28:45,906
How about Japanese food, then?

507
00:28:46,173 --> 00:28:47,922
Eating too much raw food might upset
your stomach.

508
00:28:47,946 --> 00:28:49,420
How about sukiyaki or shabu?

509
00:28:49,453 --> 00:28:50,809
Didn't you just have that yesterday?

510
00:28:50,833 --> 00:28:51,660
How about the food court upstairs?

511
00:28:51,706 --> 00:28:53,906
That's no different from eating at
the school cafeteria.

512
00:28:54,950 --> 00:28:55,950
Then…

513
00:28:56,760 --> 00:28:58,573
What do you wanna eat?

514
00:29:01,240 --> 00:29:01,893
Anything.

515
00:29:01,926 --> 00:29:02,926
Damn.

516
00:29:04,410 --> 00:29:06,726
Okay, okay. Whatever you want.

517
00:29:07,110 --> 00:29:09,640
Sorry, I don’t usually get to choose what to eat.

518
00:29:10,086 --> 00:29:11,086
Ruth!

519
00:29:11,920 --> 00:29:13,533
I knew it was you.

520
00:29:15,280 --> 00:29:17,053
Is this Ji?

521
00:29:18,340 --> 00:29:19,340
Nice to see you.

522
00:29:19,433 --> 00:29:20,000
Hello.

523
00:29:20,340 --> 00:29:21,746
I liked your gel candle.

524
00:29:22,880 --> 00:29:23,880
Thank you.

525
00:29:24,706 --> 00:29:25,706
What are you doing here?

526
00:29:25,773 --> 00:29:27,953
I told you I was coming to buy a camera today.

527
00:29:28,220 --> 00:29:30,273
Let's go eat. Mom's already inside.

528
00:29:37,010 --> 00:29:39,933
Ji, why don't you join us?

529
00:29:39,966 --> 00:29:41,293
The more, the merrier.

530
00:29:41,480 --> 00:29:43,426
I want to talk to you about Jean, too.

531
00:29:44,540 --> 00:29:45,980
- Okay.
- Yay, let’s go.

532
00:29:53,260 --> 00:29:55,260
Ji, try this duck.

533
00:29:55,640 --> 00:29:57,506
The chef here is really good.

534
00:29:57,980 --> 00:29:59,100
Ruth, serve him some.

535
00:29:59,860 --> 00:30:01,380
Go ahead. Give him a generous portion.

536
00:30:01,453 --> 00:30:02,453
It's really delicious.

537
00:30:07,950 --> 00:30:09,286
The food here is so salty.

538
00:30:10,400 --> 00:30:11,640
Eat it while it's still hot.

539
00:30:22,920 --> 00:30:24,300
How is it? Good, right?

540
00:30:25,770 --> 00:30:27,786
Mm, it's delicious. Really delicious.

541
00:30:27,820 --> 00:30:28,460
Eat up, then.

542
00:30:28,500 --> 00:30:29,860
- Serve him more.
- Okay.

543
00:30:29,900 --> 00:30:30,726
It’s just so good.
I’m good.

544
00:30:31,666 --> 00:30:32,946
- Let’s eat together.
- Don’t be shy.

545
00:30:32,970 --> 00:30:35,500
It’s my treat.

546
00:30:35,533 --> 00:30:36,902
- Eat up, you two.
- Have some duck skin.

547
00:30:36,926 --> 00:30:38,040
I’ll just eat tomatoes.

548
00:30:38,080 --> 00:30:39,786
- Don’t be shy.
- It’s okay. Eat up.

549
00:30:40,810 --> 00:30:42,066
1…2…3.

550
00:30:44,300 --> 00:30:46,300
Smile, 1…2…3.

551
00:30:49,540 --> 00:30:50,706
One more. One more.

552
00:30:52,600 --> 00:30:53,920
- 1…2…3.
- He’s just like his dad.

553
00:30:55,560 --> 00:30:56,560
Sorry?

554
00:30:59,700 --> 00:31:00,700
Ruth.

555
00:31:01,380 --> 00:31:03,153
Of all my three children,

556
00:31:03,910 --> 00:31:05,900
Ruth takes after his father the most.

557
00:31:07,160 --> 00:31:07,966
1…2…3.

558
00:31:08,006 --> 00:31:09,253
Though he seems quiet,

559
00:31:09,613 --> 00:31:10,813
he’s very picky.

560
00:31:11,510 --> 00:31:12,740
Especially with his food.

561
00:31:18,440 --> 00:31:19,666
Thank you so much, Ji.

562
00:31:21,360 --> 00:31:23,533
Me? About what, ma’am?

563
00:31:26,560 --> 00:31:28,120
Since the new semester started,

564
00:31:28,606 --> 00:31:30,706
Ruth seems so much more lively.

565
00:31:31,300 --> 00:31:32,300
That's thanks to you.

566
00:31:34,450 --> 00:31:37,906
I know about Ji, the good boy,

567
00:31:40,120 --> 00:31:42,240
and that... what was it?

568
00:31:42,266 --> 00:31:44,666
You guys splashing water at each other
in the boys' bathroom.

569
00:31:45,060 --> 00:31:46,386
Lita told me about it.

570
00:31:47,760 --> 00:31:48,922
I think that was the first time

571
00:31:48,946 --> 00:31:50,920
Ruth had ever been scolded by a teacher.

572
00:31:55,680 --> 00:31:56,680
Here.

573
00:31:57,080 --> 00:31:58,080
That means you like it?

574
00:31:59,620 --> 00:32:01,460
Though we've always lived under the same roof,

575
00:32:02,660 --> 00:32:04,433
it feels like I've got my son back.

576
00:32:07,793 --> 00:32:08,820
One more.

577
00:32:09,233 --> 00:32:10,233
Okay.

578
00:32:28,106 --> 00:32:30,100
Yo, Ji, my brother!

579
00:32:31,680 --> 00:32:32,680
Hello.

580
00:32:34,510 --> 00:32:36,646
Why are you here so early, Ji?

581
00:32:37,126 --> 00:32:38,713
How did I get here after someone who's

582
00:32:38,733 --> 00:32:40,093
been late for five years straight?

583
00:32:44,040 --> 00:32:45,367
Do I look bad?

584
00:32:45,629 --> 00:32:47,680
No, it suits you.

585
00:32:48,010 --> 00:32:49,498
- Beautiful.
- So cute.

586
00:32:52,420 --> 00:32:53,229
- Stop!
- Ouch!

587
00:32:53,250 --> 00:32:54,378
Stop it.

588
00:32:54,843 --> 00:32:57,309
You do have a way with words, just like Pim said.

589
00:32:57,352 --> 00:32:59,760
Doesn’t your hair get in the way when
you play basketball?

590
00:32:59,803 --> 00:33:02,181
No. I’m coaching this year.

591
00:33:02,669 --> 00:33:05,650
And after that, I’ll quit the basketball club.

592
00:33:09,000 --> 00:33:11,156
Seeing everyone else doing what they want,

593
00:33:11,480 --> 00:33:13,883
I don't know why I should keep forcing
myself to do this.

594
00:33:15,010 --> 00:33:16,247
Great job, Ked.

595
00:33:16,632 --> 00:33:19,410
After you quit, let’s go have egg yolk ice-cream.

596
00:33:19,738 --> 00:33:23,207
Is that all you think about, Ty?

597
00:33:24,520 --> 00:33:26,240
Come on. Let’s get to work.

598
00:33:27,020 --> 00:33:28,974
Please come in.

599
00:33:33,490 --> 00:33:35,098
Where are the school council members?

600
00:33:35,490 --> 00:33:37,161
I heard they had a meeting in the morning.

601
00:33:37,185 --> 00:33:38,185
They’ll be here after.

602
00:33:38,710 --> 00:33:39,890
What have you done?

603
00:33:40,101 --> 00:33:41,890
I said, blue. Blue.

604
00:33:42,087 --> 00:33:43,432
This is blue. See?

605
00:33:43,461 --> 00:33:45,134
That’s not blue. That’s green.

606
00:33:45,200 --> 00:33:47,403
The bucket is purple, but the paint is blue.

607
00:33:47,447 --> 00:33:48,138
Are you blind?
- It’s green.
- See?

608
00:33:49,076 --> 00:33:50,303
- It’s not green.
- Here. This is blue.

609
00:33:50,327 --> 00:33:51,614
That is dark blue.

610
00:33:51,840 --> 00:33:52,632
- That’s not blue.
- It is.

611
00:33:52,661 --> 00:33:54,305
- It’s blue. See?
- It’s green.

612
00:33:54,356 --> 00:33:55,774
Wrong. You’re wrong.

613
00:33:55,796 --> 00:33:56,356
Gun,

614
00:33:56,632 --> 00:33:58,050
don’t you have a sport practice?

615
00:33:58,087 --> 00:33:59,221
What are you doing here?

616
00:33:59,818 --> 00:34:01,220
Why can’t I be here?

617
00:34:01,374 --> 00:34:02,374
I want to be here.

618
00:34:03,083 --> 00:34:04,007
Here’s a thing.

619
00:34:04,008 --> 00:34:06,800
- Gun was in art club, right?
- Go on.

620
00:34:06,850 --> 00:34:10,545
And actually, I didn't design this colored
backdrop all by myself.

621
00:34:10,756 --> 00:34:12,058
Gun helped, too?

622
00:34:12,618 --> 00:34:14,203
Huh? Gun helped you?

623
00:34:14,429 --> 00:34:16,174
- Yes. Gun designed this.
- This one?

624
00:34:16,225 --> 00:34:17,225
Mmm.

625
00:34:18,180 --> 00:34:21,236
I can’t believe someone like Gun

626
00:34:22,720 --> 00:34:24,901
can be useful, too.

627
00:34:24,938 --> 00:34:26,647
Watch your mouth, Ler.

628
00:34:26,683 --> 00:34:28,930
Stop fighting and get this done.

629
00:34:28,967 --> 00:34:29,840
So we can go home.

630
00:34:29,970 --> 00:34:32,429
I’m sorry but I’m already home.

631
00:34:32,458 --> 00:34:33,458
Shut up.

632
00:34:35,510 --> 00:34:36,510
Guys!

633
00:34:37,900 --> 00:34:39,403
Water Dragon Attack!

634
00:34:39,432 --> 00:34:39,941
- Hey!
- Hey!

635
00:34:40,000 --> 00:34:41,416
- It’s spilling on me.
- You’re gonna mess this up, Tyler.

636
00:34:41,440 --> 00:34:42,836
You’re ruining the work.

637
00:34:43,090 --> 00:34:44,203
Hey! Oh, no.

638
00:34:47,890 --> 00:34:49,076
Damn it, Ler!

639
00:34:49,112 --> 00:34:50,443
I’m sorry, bro!

640
00:34:50,487 --> 00:34:52,414
I’m sorry. Help me!

641
00:34:52,450 --> 00:34:53,621
Ji, help me!

642
00:34:55,643 --> 00:34:56,829
Ji, help me, Ji.

643
00:34:56,850 --> 00:34:59,643
- Please, no, no, no.
- Take this.

644
00:35:01,720 --> 00:35:02,887
There you go.

645
00:35:12,340 --> 00:35:14,290
Take this. Take this.

646
00:35:18,940 --> 00:35:21,905
Guys, here comes the food.

647
00:35:22,225 --> 00:35:23,709
Come and eat.

648
00:35:23,745 --> 00:35:25,716
Come on. Here are the chopsticks and plates.

649
00:35:25,745 --> 00:35:27,621
Hey, I’m hungry. Let me have some.

650
00:35:28,070 --> 00:35:29,070
Hey, come on, come on.

651
00:35:29,280 --> 00:35:30,596
Come on now.

652
00:35:36,100 --> 00:35:37,280
- Wow.
- Wow.

653
00:35:37,316 --> 00:35:37,905
Oh my gosh.

654
00:35:37,941 --> 00:35:38,941
You’re not eating?

655
00:35:39,076 --> 00:35:40,680
No, I’m not hungry.

656
00:35:42,420 --> 00:35:43,876
You’re late, Mr. President.

657
00:35:46,050 --> 00:35:47,127
I had to finish something.

658
00:35:47,730 --> 00:35:48,807
About the Sports Day?

659
00:35:50,940 --> 00:35:52,116
It’s not that.

660
00:35:55,890 --> 00:35:58,170
The teacher entered me in the science
project competition.

661
00:35:58,580 --> 00:36:00,414
My name has already been submitted,

662
00:36:00,887 --> 00:36:01,887
so I can’t withdraw.

663
00:36:03,300 --> 00:36:04,380
Will it take the whole day?

664
00:36:04,516 --> 00:36:05,890
My competition is in the morning.

665
00:36:07,390 --> 00:36:09,150
By the time everyone else finishes competing

666
00:36:10,480 --> 00:36:11,745
and I get back to school,

667
00:36:12,116 --> 00:36:13,436
Sports Day will probably be over.

668
00:36:15,330 --> 00:36:16,407
It’s okay.

669
00:36:16,989 --> 00:36:18,400
It’s just Sports Day.

670
00:36:18,669 --> 00:36:20,610
You still have the Open House to work on.

671
00:36:21,112 --> 00:36:22,116
Don’t worry too much.

672
00:36:27,810 --> 00:36:28,996
There’s paint on your face.

673
00:36:29,540 --> 00:36:30,058
Really?

674
00:36:30,385 --> 00:36:32,050
- Where is the paint…
- Hey.

675
00:36:32,580 --> 00:36:33,580
Don’t touch.

676
00:36:33,796 --> 00:36:34,876
You’re gonna make it worse.

677
00:36:42,189 --> 00:36:43,189
Uh...

678
00:36:43,540 --> 00:36:46,007
Why are your hands so sticky?

679
00:36:47,460 --> 00:36:48,698
Don't tell me...

680
00:36:48,734 --> 00:36:50,734
The hand you're using to wipe me with

681
00:36:50,763 --> 00:36:53,047
is the same hand you used to hold that paintbrush.

682
00:36:58,770 --> 00:37:00,763
I'm not getting messy all by myself!

683
00:37:00,800 --> 00:37:01,978
No, no, no.

684
00:37:02,378 --> 00:37:03,378
Come here.

685
00:37:03,832 --> 00:37:04,832
No, no, no, no.

686
00:37:05,425 --> 00:37:06,210
Hey, what’s that?
What?

687
00:37:07,323 --> 00:37:08,625
I’m not gonna fall for that.

688
00:37:08,800 --> 00:37:09,898
Stop, stop, stop!

689
00:37:10,465 --> 00:37:11,465
- Stop, stop!
- No.

690
00:37:12,740 --> 00:37:13,694
- Yes.
- No, no, no,

691
00:37:13,723 --> 00:37:15,432
- Yes.
- No, no, no, no, no, no.

692
00:37:16,490 --> 00:37:17,243
- See you.
- See you.

693
00:37:17,287 --> 00:37:18,567
Thank you. Thanks a lot.

694
00:37:18,589 --> 00:37:19,876
- Bye-bye.
- Bye-bye.

695
00:37:20,072 --> 00:37:21,658
- See you later.
- See you. Bye.

696
00:37:21,687 --> 00:37:22,687
Bye-bye.

697
00:37:31,200 --> 00:37:32,960
Ruth, your car’s here.

698
00:37:33,352 --> 00:37:34,130
Bye-bye.

699
00:37:34,160 --> 00:37:35,570
See you tomorrow.

700
00:37:35,985 --> 00:37:36,985
Mmm.

701
00:37:37,345 --> 00:37:38,345
See you.

702
00:37:51,530 --> 00:37:53,229
Wow, Ji, look at that.

703
00:37:54,320 --> 00:37:55,320
Look at what?

704
00:37:55,861 --> 00:37:57,701
It's just like the drama I watched last night.

705
00:37:58,600 --> 00:38:00,545
The girl marries into the guy's family,

706
00:38:00,567 --> 00:38:02,043
but his parents don’t like her.

707
00:38:02,625 --> 00:38:03,625
Exactly.

708
00:38:03,825 --> 00:38:04,825
Tyler!

709
00:38:05,090 --> 00:38:06,090
Look at his face.

710
00:38:06,850 --> 00:38:08,560
I’ll go home, then.

711
00:38:08,596 --> 00:38:09,869
- See you tomorrow.
- See you.

712
00:38:10,480 --> 00:38:11,047
Bye-bye.

713
00:38:11,440 --> 00:38:12,440
See you later.

714
00:38:18,540 --> 00:38:19,818
Was that boy Jira’s son?

715
00:38:25,540 --> 00:38:26,540
Yes.

716
00:38:30,870 --> 00:38:33,270
Are you withdrawing from the competition
because of that boy?

717
00:38:54,800 --> 00:38:55,876
(Morning, Ji.)

718
00:38:55,927 --> 00:38:57,360
Did that hurt?

719
00:38:57,556 --> 00:38:59,832
You said you wanted to show me something.

720
00:39:02,740 --> 00:39:04,865
Ta da!

721
00:39:08,650 --> 00:39:10,341
Why aren’t you excited?

722
00:39:11,230 --> 00:39:12,230
Oh!

723
00:39:12,320 --> 00:39:13,320
Wow!

724
00:39:14,350 --> 00:39:16,065
That phone is so cool!

725
00:39:16,283 --> 00:39:17,883
Look. It can do this.

726
00:39:18,261 --> 00:39:19,563
With this bad boy,

727
00:39:19,614 --> 00:39:21,560
we can FaceTime each other whenever we want.

728
00:39:22,740 --> 00:39:24,786
But we’re already seeing each other’s
face all day long.

729
00:39:24,810 --> 00:39:26,589
Because you don’t have this,

730
00:39:27,010 --> 00:39:28,570
your relationship’s not going anywhere.

731
00:39:29,350 --> 00:39:30,916
Thanks for your advice.

732
00:39:31,265 --> 00:39:32,265
But I didn’t need it.

733
00:39:34,880 --> 00:39:36,130
Hey, how do you have this?

734
00:39:36,741 --> 00:39:38,960
It’s brand new. I just got it.

735
00:39:39,003 --> 00:39:40,509
Does it have eFootball?

736
00:39:40,530 --> 00:39:41,576
There’s only this. Jump, jump.

737
00:39:41,600 --> 00:39:42,909
You have to get in line, Gun.

738
00:39:43,047 --> 00:39:45,425
No, no, no, no. Hey, hey, hey.

739
00:39:45,469 --> 00:39:46,676
Hula Hula Hooray

740
00:39:46,712 --> 00:39:48,000
Hooray Hooray Hula

741
00:39:48,036 --> 00:39:50,472
Go, Red, Go

742
00:39:50,509 --> 00:39:51,534
Hooray Hooray Hula

743
00:39:51,563 --> 00:39:52,625
Hooray Hooray Hula

744
00:39:52,654 --> 00:39:53,869
Go, Red, Go

745
00:40:10,000 --> 00:40:11,512
I’m Kwan from Class 2.

746
00:40:12,670 --> 00:40:14,130
I’m Ji from Class 7.

747
00:40:14,174 --> 00:40:15,054
I know.

748
00:40:15,098 --> 00:40:16,770
Your name is on your shirt.

749
00:40:19,287 --> 00:40:20,287
Ji.

750
00:40:20,710 --> 00:40:21,170
Hey,

751
00:40:21,192 --> 00:40:22,232
What are you doing here?

752
00:40:22,269 --> 00:40:23,403
I was just walking around.

753
00:40:23,796 --> 00:40:25,338
I should ask you. What are you doing here?

754
00:40:25,352 --> 00:40:28,261
The student council hasn't had much work lately.

755
00:40:28,305 --> 00:40:29,963
Mmm. By the way…

756
00:40:33,450 --> 00:40:34,836
Kwan is back to playing ping pong.

757
00:40:37,781 --> 00:40:39,780
You know Kwan?

758
00:40:40,170 --> 00:40:41,170
Yeah.

759
00:40:43,025 --> 00:40:44,203
The drama club president.

760
00:40:45,890 --> 00:40:47,105
Oh.

761
00:40:49,530 --> 00:40:50,974
The stage play.

762
00:40:52,660 --> 00:40:53,660
Mmm.

763
00:40:54,880 --> 00:40:56,785
Where are you going after school?

764
00:40:57,410 --> 00:40:59,716
I’ll leave at 3 p.m.

765
00:41:00,247 --> 00:41:02,865
I have to take Tyler to rent some new manga
near my house today.

766
00:41:07,141 --> 00:41:08,141
Wanna come with us?

767
00:41:10,327 --> 00:41:12,465
- Sure.
- Let’s go.

768
00:41:20,610 --> 00:41:22,378
Hi, Ji, Ty.

769
00:41:22,407 --> 00:41:24,123
- Hello.
- Has your school started?

770
00:41:24,552 --> 00:41:26,120
Yes. This is our first day.

771
00:41:26,152 --> 00:41:27,047
Ah.

772
00:41:27,069 --> 00:41:29,040
Have the new mangas arrived yet?

773
00:41:29,069 --> 00:41:30,138
Yeah, they’re here.

774
00:41:32,130 --> 00:41:32,749
Here.

775
00:41:33,090 --> 00:41:34,090
Thank you.

776
00:41:34,770 --> 00:41:35,896
There's an old horror manga I've been wanting

777
00:41:35,920 --> 00:41:37,643
to get my hands on, Chok.

778
00:41:37,687 --> 00:41:38,687
Do you have it?

779
00:41:43,760 --> 00:41:44,760
Hey.

780
00:41:45,280 --> 00:41:46,280
Is this the one?

781
00:41:46,690 --> 00:41:47,483
It’s not.

782
00:41:47,520 --> 00:41:50,160
This one came out two years before
the volume Tyler is looking for.

783
00:41:53,230 --> 00:41:55,003
Hey, is it this one?

784
00:41:55,025 --> 00:41:56,036
Oh, yes.

785
00:42:26,640 --> 00:42:28,392
Ji, what happened? I’m here.

786
00:42:31,860 --> 00:42:32,860
Nothing.

787
00:42:33,061 --> 00:42:34,909
I’ve found the manga you’re looking for.

788
00:42:35,240 --> 00:42:37,883
Don’t come in here. There’s no space.

789
00:42:58,720 --> 00:43:00,552
Hey, Ji, what happened?

790
00:43:00,596 --> 00:43:01,881
Why did you just leave Ruth in there?

791
00:43:01,905 --> 00:43:03,840
Are you two fighting?

792
00:43:05,740 --> 00:43:08,516
Hey, why are your ears so red?

793
00:43:12,230 --> 00:43:14,603
It’s you who came into my life

794
00:43:14,640 --> 00:43:17,309
You light up my new beginning

795
00:43:17,352 --> 00:43:19,629
Once weary heart, you make it full

796
00:43:19,672 --> 00:43:22,036
Oh, don’t tell me you…

797
00:43:22,065 --> 00:43:25,192
Of hope with the love from you

798
00:43:25,214 --> 00:43:28,894
Turning my world into a dream come true

799
00:43:28,923 --> 00:43:30,530
It’s you who came into my life

800
00:43:30,567 --> 00:43:32,916
You light up my new beginning

801
00:43:33,498 --> 00:43:34,305
Stop it.

802
00:43:34,334 --> 00:43:37,440
Because of you, I want to keep going
-You’ve got your manga. Now go home. Bye.

803
00:43:37,498 --> 00:43:41,978
Whatever fate may bring, whatever is in store

804
00:43:42,007 --> 00:43:45,716
In you, I find hope once more

805
00:44:16,430 --> 00:44:17,767
Once we cross that finish line,

806
00:44:18,730 --> 00:44:20,050
we won't be just friends anymore.

807
00:44:25,680 --> 00:44:27,490
I won the science project competition.

808
00:44:27,890 --> 00:44:28,890
Where's my reward?
